# g2.conf.allow — TCR-CFG-001 locked-down allow-list for the auto-generated
# qvm guest config (g2.conf).
#
# Phase 1 (study-level). validate-g2conf.sh validates the g2.conf emitted by
# post_start.custom against this allow-list BEFORE `qvm @g2.conf` runs, and
# fails CLOSED on any directive whose leading keyword is not listed here.
# This is the implementable FLOOR (validate-against-locked-template).
#
#   study-only ceiling: in a real programme the config would additionally be
#   cryptographically SIGNED and the signature verified against a key in a
#   hardware-backed store before qvm consumes it. No RoT exists on the TCG
#   leg, so signing is NOT implemented here (see TCR-CFG-001 / TCR-SB-001).
#
# Format: one allowed directive keyword per line. A g2.conf line is allowed
# iff its first whitespace-delimited token (after leading indentation) is in
# this set. '#' comments and blank lines ignored. Matching is exact on the
# keyword; this bounds WHICH directives may ever appear, implementing
# least-vdev (TCR-HYP-001): any vdev/keyword not listed is forbidden.
#
# Keywords below are exactly those emitted by the no-network g2.conf in
# post_start.custom. virtio-net is intentionally NOT allowed (least-vdev /
# inert net path). Adding a keyword here is a reviewed config-surface change.

# --- allowed directive keywords (first token of a g2.conf line) ---
system
ram
cpu
load
vdev
hostdev
loc
intr
name

# --- allowed vdev TYPES (second token of a 'vdev <type>' line) ---
# Prefixed 'vdev:' so the validator can enforce least-vdev at the type level,
# not just the keyword level: 'vdev passthru' is rejected even though 'vdev'
# is an allowed keyword. virtio-net is intentionally absent (inert net path /
# TCR-HYP-001 least-vdev).
vdev:pl011
vdev:virtio-console
vdev:virtio-blk
